From b74b1d149cb8bd360a6d101ccd7512217635c34f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:17:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(scratchpad): never reframe a member when a pad is
 shown

Showing a scratchpad moved any member whose centre lay outside the pad's usable area to the exact centre of that area.
That test contradicted the floating margin, which lets a window hang off an edge as long as part of it stays
grabbable: a 400x240 member at x = -300 (100 px visible, inside the margin) was teleported to 440,240 on a 1280x720
output, on every first show and therefore on every reopen.

A show now presents members where they are. The framing policy stays where the floating settle put it, and a pad that
changes output keeps remapping its members in moveScratchpad(), which also carries the area a pad was last sized
against while every output is absent.

tests/harness/checks/scratchpad/reopen_keeps_position.sh pins both: the hanging-off member keeps -300,100 across
show, hide and reopen (440,240 before), and a pad shown on the second output lands the member at that output's edge
(1280,100) instead of its centre (1720,240).

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
