From eda5ca858233d7ea07fdf42509b965758302e645 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 00:49:19 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(scratchpad): carry an arriving window into the pad's
 own output

Review of the show-reframing fix found two places where a pad could still
leak another output's coordinates onto the output it shows on.

A window moved into a pad that already shows on a different output kept the
coordinates of the output it arrived on. The pad presents it on its own
output, so the window could sit off screen for as long as the pad stayed
shown. Admission now remaps it from the arrival output's usable area into the
pad's, the same proportional remap a member gets when the pad changes output.

A member restored to an output that went away and came back used the plain
product of its saved fraction and the new box. The fraction is proportional
but the grabbable margin is a fixed band, so a wider replacement scaled a
legal hanging position past the margin and left the window out of reach.
The restore goes through the same clamp as every other floating restore.

tests/harness/checks/scratchpad/reopen_keeps_position.sh pins both: a window
focused on the first output joins a pad already showing on the second
(100,100 before), and a member hanging at x = -300 off an 800x600 output
comes back at -325 instead of -600 when a 1600x900 output replaces it.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
