From aa40f58722c17756b7901a3b7e591892bb6dad71 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ZhangDM-520 <jixianqiang1540@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 01:25:32 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(scratchpad): remap only a window the user moves into
 a showing pad

The admit-time remap ran for every admission that arrived from another
output, which fought the two paths that place a window themselves.

A window that is still opening is placed by View::handleMap() against the
pad's output after admission, so an output that differs from the one the
window arrived on is expected there: remapping it scaled a proportional
window a second time, by the ratio of the two usable areas, and centred the
placement on a size the window no longer had. A rule admission is followed
by its own summon back to the rule's output, so remapping it into the pad's
current output first and then back out clamped the overhang away.

The remap now applies to an interactive admission of an already-placed
window: the one shape where the pad presents a window the user moved into
it somewhere else, and nothing else places it.

tests/harness/checks/scratchpad/reopen_keeps_position.sh pins it: a
proportional pad showing on another output opens a 600x400 window at
600x400 (480x320 before). The check also stops recreating the connector a
pad was displaced from, so the replacement-output leg now fails at
1280,1380 instead of only passing through the displaced restore, and it
asserts the exact margin and basis positions instead of one-sided bounds.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
